# Paths chezmoi should delete from the target if present.
#
# Session units moved from graphical-session.target to wayland-session@sway.target
# so they stop under any compositor other than sway. Without this, the old enable
# symlinks stay behind on already-installed machines and the leak persists.
.config/systemd/user/graphical-session.target.wants

# Wallpapers used to be shipped as tracked PNGs, one per theme. They are now
# generated on the machine and named <theme>-<style>.png, so the old files are
# no longer written by anything and would otherwise sit in the target directory
# forever - chezmoi leaves files it does not manage alone rather than deleting
# them.
#
# The generated ones are deliberately NOT listed here. They are a cache: losing
# them costs a second and a half each, but chezmoi removing them on every apply
# would mean regenerating on every sync.
.local/share/wallpapers/deep-violet.png
.local/share/wallpapers/neon.png
.local/share/wallpapers/ember.png
.local/share/wallpapers/slate.png

# xdg-terminal-exec moved to /usr/local/bin, installed by apply-config.sh.
# glib looks it up by name on PATH, and ~/.local/bin is not on the session PATH
# - so the copy here was never found, and leaving it would be a second one to
# wonder about.
.local/bin/xdg-terminal-exec

# The shortcut viewer was a rofi mode before it became a window, and rofi
# themes are only read by rofi. Left behind it would be a file nobody could
# explain.
.config/rofi/shortcuts.rasi

# sway-place-floating scored positions for a new floating window and moved it to
# the emptiest one. Removed on TASK-54: placement can only happen after the
# window exists, so it appeared centred and then jumped, which read as a glitch
# on every login. The greeting card is centred by a window rule instead.
.local/bin/sway-place-floating

# Two environment.d files this repository deleted and then left behind on every
# machine that already had them. TASK-94.
#
# 10-cursor.conf had its contents folded into 10-appearance.conf in 87abc7c.
# Leaving it was not harmless: the user manager reads *.conf in lexicographic
# order and the last one wins, so 10-cursor sorts AFTER 10-appearance and its
# copy of XCURSOR_THEME and XCURSOR_SIZE overrode the managed file - on machines
# that had it, and not on a fresh one. A difference between the running system
# and a rebuild that no diff would show.
#
# 20-path.conf was deleted in ea2af45, the commit that established environment.d
# cannot prepend to PATH and moved xdg-terminal-exec to /usr/local/bin instead.
# Measured inert here - the user manager's PATH contains no ~/.local/bin and no
# unexpanded $PATH - but a file arguing at length for a mechanism the repository
# has since disproved is worse than no file.
.config/environment.d/10-cursor.conf
.config/environment.d/20-path.conf

# greeting.service opened a terminal on login and on every empty workspace.
# TASK-113: it had become more annoying than useful, so the whole mechanism -
# the unit, its wants symlink, and the helper script that watched sway for an
# empty workspace - is gone rather than merely toggled off.
.config/systemd/user/greeting.service
.config/systemd/user/wayland-session@sway.target.wants/greeting.service
.local/bin/sway-workspace-greeter
